      "title": "A MEC remains life insurance with different access rules",
      "narration": "Marcus wants to pay a large premium into a cash-value life policy. The funding pattern can affect whether it becomes a modified endowment contract, usually called a MEC. A MEC still meets the federal definition of life insurance, but it fails the applicable seven-pay funding test or comes from an exchange of another MEC. Its living distributions receive different tax treatment. MEC status does not, by itself, remove the ordinary income-tax exclusion for a qualifying death benefit. Nor does it automatically require annual tax on all inside growth. Identify the transaction: paying a premium, receiving a withdrawal, taking a loan or receiving a death payment.",
